    "updated_at": "2017-08-21T18:47:59Z",
    "body": "All input types are at least \"semi-replaced\". We're still not really sure how that state works; it's not fully a replaced element (it doesn't size like one, and responds to some properties), but still has some notion of an \"intrinsic\" size that it likes to obey (unlike normal elements) and is unbreakable.\r\n\r\nThat example of an inline <input> breaking across lines would unfortunately be a complete break with current web compatibility.\r\n\r\n(So yeah, bug 23893 is def still waiting on me, but the CSSWG in general doesn't know the answer to it yet. fantasai and I will move toward defining it eventually...)",
