    "updated_at": "2017-08-21T20:40:34Z",
    "body": "Doesn't matter if it's more annoying or not (it definitely is!). It's required for web compat. Buttons *never* linebreak, even if they are set to `display:inline` and have multiple words in their value. Same with inputs/etc.  It's 100% certain that there is content on the web that depends on this, as it's been dependable for decades.\r\n\r\n(Tangent: Why are you spelling it \"quirx\"? It's \"quirks\", as in the plural of \"quirk\".)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
